# [[ title .Name ]]

A [Quanarch](https://quanarch.org) project.

```
[[ .Name ]]/
├── packages/
│   └── [[ (index .Quas 0).Name ]]/      qua: the contract between the quanar and its quans
├── quanar/                 quanar: loads the quans and plugs in the qua
└── quans/
    └── [[ (index .Quans 0).Name ]]/      quan: business logic, loaded by the quanar
```

## Run

In two terminals:

```sh
cd quans/[[ (index .Quans 0).Name ]] && npm run watch     # builds the quan and serves it on port [[ (index .Quans 0).Port ]]
cd quanar && npm run dev               # starts the quanar on port 5173
```

Open http://localhost:5173/[[ (index .Quans 0).Name ]]

The counter on the page belongs to the quan, but the quan never adds to it
itself: it calls `increment` on the qua, and the quanar does the counting.
